%T A400995 4481,5051,5813,5827,6563,7489,8563,8573,8609,8837,9883,10513,11633,
%U A400995 11783,11833,12037,12923,13397,14827,14969,15493,16487,17167,18059,18341,18899,19727
%N A400995 Prime numbers p such that p^4 is an interprime = average of two successive primes.
%H A400995 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PrimeGaps.html">Prime Gaps</a>.
%e A400995 211 is a term because prevprime(211^4) = 1982119423, nextprime(211^4) = 1982119459, and 1982119423 + 1982119459 = 2*211^4.
%o A400995 (PARI) isok(p) = if (isprime(p), precprime(p^4-1) + nextprime(p^4+1) == 2*p^4);
%o A400995 select(isok, primes(3000)) \\ _Michel Marcus_, Oct 29 2026
%Y A400995 Cf. A030514 (primes^4), A006512 (prime gaps).
%Y A400995 Cf. A123993 (for p^2), A248799 (for p^3).
